Seller: It''s two hundred yuan. The silk is of very high quality.
Lin: That sounds a bit expensive for me. Could you lower the price?
Seller: Well, how much are you willing to pay for it?
Lin: I was thinking about one hundred and forty yuan.
Seller: That''s too low. But because business is slow today, I can offer one hundred and seventy.
Lin: How about one hundred and sixty, and I''ll take two of them?
Seller: All right, it''s a deal. Two scarves for three hundred and twenty yuan.', '林问丝巾多少钱;卖家要价二百元,说丝绸质量很好;林觉得贵,请求降价;卖家问她愿出多少;林想出一百四;卖家说太低,但因今天生意清淡可降到一百七;林提出一百六并买两条;卖家同意,两条共三百二十元成交。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does Lin want to buy?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A silk scarf.","A pair of shoes.","A gold ring.","A leather bag."]},{"q":"What is the seller''s first price for one scarf?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["One hundred and forty yuan.","Two hundred yuan.","One hundred and seventy yuan.","Three hundred and twenty yuan."]},{"q":"Why does the seller agree to lower the price?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Because business is slow today.","Because the scarf is of poor quality.","Because Lin is a close friend.","Because the shop is closing forever."]},{"q":"How much does Lin first offer to pay?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["One hundred and sixty yuan.","One hundred and forty yuan.","One hundred and seventy yuan.","Two hundred yuan."]},{"q":"What is the final deal they reach?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["One scarf for two hundred yuan.","Three scarves for free.","Two scarves for three hundred and twenty yuan.","One scarf for one hundred and forty yuan."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U2', 'sufe');
When they spend money on hotels, food and shopping abroad, they help create jobs in those places.
In 2017, Chinese tourists made more than one hundred million trips overseas.
This spending is good for the countries they visit, and it is also a kind of trade.
As more people travel, the world becomes more closely connected.', '每年有数百万中国游客出国;他们在国外的住宿、餐饮和购物花费帮助当地创造就业;2017年中国游客出境超过一亿人次;这种花费有利于所到国家,也是一种贸易;随着更多人出行,世界联系更紧密。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"Who travels abroad each year, according to the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only a few rich people.","Only government officials.","Nobody at all.","Millions of Chinese travellers."]},{"q":"How does their spending help other countries?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["It helps create jobs there.","It closes local shops.","It makes hotels empty.","It stops local trade."]},{"q":"How many overseas trips did Chinese tourists make in 2017?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["About one hundred.","More than one hundred million.","Fewer than ten.","Exactly one thousand."]},{"q":"What is tourist spending described as?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A kind of tax.","A waste of money.","A kind of trade.","A type of farming."]},{"q":"What happens as more people travel?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The world becomes more divided.","Trade comes to an end.","Travel becomes impossible.","The world becomes more closely connected."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U2', 'sufe');
Manager: I''m very sorry to hear that. Let me have a look at it.
Customer: I''ve already tried charging it all night, and nothing happens.
Manager: You''re right, it does seem broken. Would you like a free repair?
Customer: Considering all the trouble, I''d prefer a new phone or my money back.
Manager: I understand. I can give you a brand-new phone of the same model.
Customer: That sounds fair. Thank you for solving it so quickly.
Manager: It was our mistake, so there is no charge at all.', '顾客说昨天买的手机开不了机;经理道歉并查看;顾客说已充了一整夜电仍无反应;经理承认手机坏了,提出免费维修;顾客考虑到麻烦,更想换新机或退款;经理同意换一部同型号新机;顾客觉得公道并致谢;经理说是店里的过错,不收任何费用。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What problem does the customer have?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["The phone won''t turn on.","The phone is too expensive.","The phone is the wrong colour.","The phone is too small."]},{"q":"What had the customer already tried?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Selling it online.","Charging it all night.","Dropping it in water.","Giving it away."]},{"q":"What does the manager first offer?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A full refund at once.","A free meal.","A free repair.","A new colour."]},{"q":"What does the customer ask for instead?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Only a free repair.","A free phone case.","Nothing at all.","A new phone or a refund."]},{"q":"What does the manager finally agree to give?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["A brand-new phone of the same model.","An older, cheaper phone.","Only an apology.","Half of the money back."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U2', 'sufe');
Suppose you spend a whole afternoon playing games.
The real cost is not zero; it is the homework you did not finish or the book you did not read.
Economists call this the opportunity cost.
Thinking about this hidden cost helps us make wiser choices every day.', '你做的每个选择都有隐藏成本;假设你花整个下午打游戏;真正的成本不是零,而是没写完的作业或没读的书;经济学家称之为机会成本;考虑这种隐藏成本能帮我们每天做出更明智的选择。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does every choice have, according to the speaker?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["No cost at all.","A hidden cost.","A free gift.","A fixed price."]},{"q":"If you play games all afternoon, what is the real cost?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Nothing whatsoever.","The money you earn.","The homework or reading you give up.","The new friends you make."]},{"q":"What do economists call this kind of cost?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["The yearly tax.","The ticket price.","The interest rate.","The opportunity cost."]},{"q":"What does thinking about the hidden cost help us do?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Make wiser choices.","Spend without thinking.","Forget our homework.","Avoid all decisions."]},{"q":"How long does the example afternoon of games last?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Only five minutes.","A whole afternoon.","A full week.","One short hour."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U2', 'sufe');
Tom: How much more does the new one cost?
Mei: About a thousand yuan more than I had planned to spend.
Tom: Is the new phone really a thousand yuan better than your old one?
Mei: Hmm, when you put it that way, maybe not.
Tom: You could save that money for your summer trip instead.
Mei: You''re right. The extra features just aren''t worth the extra cost.
Tom: That''s smart thinking. Your old phone is still good enough.', '梅说旧手机还能用,但很想要新款;汤姆问新机贵多少;梅说比预算多约一千元;汤姆问新机真比旧机好一千元吗;梅说这么一想也许不值;汤姆建议把钱留作暑假旅行;梅认同,额外功能不值额外成本;汤姆夸她想得明智,旧手机仍够用。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does Mei want at the start?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["A new summer trip.","A cheaper old phone.","The new phone model.","A larger schoolbag."]},{"q":"How much more does the new phone cost?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Exactly the same as the old one.","About ten yuan more.","Nothing extra at all.","About a thousand yuan more than planned."]},{"q":"What question does Tom ask Mei to think about?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Whether the new phone is worth the extra cost.","Whether she likes the colour.","Whether the shop is open.","Whether Tom can borrow it."]},{"q":"What does Tom suggest doing with the money?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Buying two new phones.","Saving it for her summer trip.","Giving it all to him.","Throwing it away."]},{"q":"What does Mei finally decide?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["She must buy the new phone today.","Her old phone is useless now.","The extra features aren''t worth the extra cost.","She will never use a phone again."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'long', 'elective4', 'U2', 'sufe');
Imagine you put one yuan into the bank.
The bank can lend that yuan to a builder, who pays it to a worker.
The worker then spends it at a shop, and the shopkeeper saves it in the bank again.
In this way, a single coin can help many different people earn a living.', '钱不会静止,它在整个经济中流动;假设你把一元存进银行;银行可把它借给建筑工,后者付给工人;工人在商店花掉,店主又存进银行;这样一枚硬币能帮助许多不同的人谋生。', 'uk_female', '[{"q":"What does money do, according to the passage?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["It always stays in one place.","It quickly disappears.","It loses all its value.","It travels through the economy."]},{"q":"What can the bank do with the yuan you save?","type":"choice","answer":"A","options":["Lend it to a builder.","Burn it for fun.","Hide it forever.","Send it abroad by post."]},{"q":"After the worker is paid, what does the worker do with the money?","type":"choice","answer":"B","options":["Buries it underground.","Spends it at a shop.","Tears it into pieces.","Returns it to the builder."]},{"q":"What can a single coin do, according to the speaker?","type":"choice","answer":"C","options":["Stop all trade at once.","Make everyone poorer.","Help many people earn a living.","Be used only one time."]},{"q":"Where does the shopkeeper put the money at the end?","type":"choice","answer":"D","options":["Into the sea.","Onto the street.","Into a fire.","Back into the bank."]}]'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, 'short', 'elective4', 'U2', 'sufe');

