第1句 核心:Most decisions are small steps called marginal changes.
第2句 方法:Compare the extra benefit of one more step with its extra cost.
第3句 结论:Act only when the added benefit outweighs the added cost.
第4句 收束:Thinking at the margin helps people decide better.', 2, 'elective4', 'U2', 'sufe');

